---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
	title="Uses | Itziar Morales"
	description="Hardware, software, and self-hosted services I use daily."
>
	<p class="eyebrow">~/uses</p>
	<h1>Uses</h1>
	<p class="intro">
		The machines and software I actually use, in the spirit of
		<a href="https://uses.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener">uses.tech</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Desktop</h2>
	<p>
		Self-built, like every PC in this house &mdash; picking parts is half the fun.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>CPU:</strong> Intel Core i9-9900K &mdash; a 2018 chip that still refuses to be the bottleneck</li>
		<li><strong>GPU:</strong> NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060</li>
		<li><strong>RAM / board:</strong> 32&nbsp;GB on a Gigabyte Z390 D</li>
		<li><strong>OS:</strong> CachyOS Linux with KDE Plasma on Wayland</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Laptop</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Machine:</strong> ThinkPad P1 Gen 7 &mdash; RTX 4070, 32&nbsp;GB RAM, 2&times;1&nbsp;TB NVMe</li>
		<li><strong>OS:</strong> dual boot, Fedora + Windows &mdash; one drive each, no arguments</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Software</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Editor:</strong> Vim, with dotfiles I tinker with more than I probably should</li>
		<li><strong>Terminal life:</strong> Bash, Git, and a window-manager config that is never quite finished</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Server</h2>
	<p>
		A Hetzner box that keeps me honest about deployment, backups, and what "it works on my machine"
		really means:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Nextcloud</strong> &mdash; files and sync</li>
		<li><strong>Navidrome</strong> &mdash; music streaming</li>
		<li><strong>BookLore</strong> &mdash; the library behind the <a href="/log">reading log</a></li>
	</ul>

	<style>
		.eyebrow {
			font-family: var(--font-mono);
			color: var(--accent);
			font-size: 0.85rem;
			margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
			margin-top: 0;
		}
		.intro {
			color: var(--text-muted);
		}
		h2 {
			font-family: var(--font-mono);
			font-size: 0.95em;
			color: var(--accent);
			margin-top: 2.4em;
			padding-bottom: 0.4em;
			border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
		}
		h2::before {
			content: '## ';
			color: var(--text-muted);
		}
		ul {
			padding-left: 1.25em;
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 0.3em;
		}
		li {
			font-size: 0.92em;
		}
		li strong {
			color: var(--accent);
		}
	</style>
</PageLayout>
